---
import TextPage from '../components/TextPage.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';

const { owner, country, lastUpdated } = site.legal;
---
<TextPage
  title="Terms of Use"
  path="/terms/"
  updated={lastUpdated}
  description={`The terms for using ${site.url.replace('https://', '')}: music and artwork rights, demo submissions, bookings, links and liability.`}
>
  <p>
    These terms apply when you use {site.url.replace('https://', '')} (the "site"), run by {owner}. By using the site you
    agree to them. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Music, videos and artwork</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Songs, recordings, music videos, artwork, photos and artist names shown on the site belong to the artists, labels
      and other rights holders who own them. Several releases on this site were released by other labels; each release
      page names its label where that is the case.
    </li>
    <li>
      Videos are shown through YouTube's embedded player and remain the property of their owners. Watching them is also
      subject to <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouTube's Terms of Service</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      The site's design, text and code belong to {owner}, except where stated otherwise.
    </li>
    <li>
      You may listen, watch and share links to pages for personal, non-commercial use. You may not copy, download,
      re-upload, sell or otherwise reuse the music, videos or artwork without permission from the rights holder.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Sending us a demo</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Only send music you wrote or recorded, or have the right to share.</li>
    <li>You keep all rights to your music. Sending a demo does not transfer any rights to us.</li>
    <li>
      We listen to everything, but we cannot promise a reply, a release or any deal. Any agreement only exists once it is
      made in writing and signed by both sides.
    </li>
    <li>
      We hear a lot of music. If we later release something that sounds similar to your idea, that does not mean it was
      taken from your demo.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Shows, tickets and bookings</h2>
  <p>
    Shows, tickets and studio bookings are arranged by email or through the ticket seller named on the show. Dates,
    line-ups, venues and prices can change; the final details are the ones we confirm to you directly.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Do not try to break, overload or gain unauthorised access to the site, and do not use it for anything unlawful.
    Search engines and AI assistants are welcome to read and link to the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    The site links to YouTube, streaming services and social networks. We do not control those sites and are not
    responsible for their content or practices.
  </p>

  <h2>No guarantees</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep the site accurate and online, but it is provided "as is". We do not guarantee that it will always be
    available, error-free, or that every detail is current.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, {owner} is not liable for any indirect or consequential loss arising from use of the
    site. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
  </p>

  <h2>Copyright concerns</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe something on the site uses your work without permission, email
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with the page address and details, and we will look into it
    promptly.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and law</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms; the date at the top shows the latest version. These terms are governed by the laws of
    {country}. Questions: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>
</TextPage>
